{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity","id":248035,"title":"New Orleans Theories: Donovan's Identity","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-09-03T11:34:13-07:00","id":248035,"title":"New Orleans Theories: Donovan's Identity","content":"Out of courtsey I'm going to warn any New Orleans PCs unfamiliar with the book. This discussion contains several potential SPOILERS to the New Orleans setting. You have been warned...<br /> <br /> Hey everyone, I'm planning on running a pre-hurricane New Orleans chronicle and recently got my hands on the book. I've been reading through the cast thoroughly but there was one thing I couldn't find. In both Donovan's description and Gabriel Hursts' they mention that Sheriff Donovan has a very dirty secret. They discuss how Donovan used to go by the fake name Donovan Gage in both life and death. However he dropped the last name as part of his identity early on as a neonate, leaving only Savoy, Vidal, and Maldonato remembering he ever even went by this false last name. Apparently the sheriff is quite nervous about people digging into his past in case they learn who he really is.<br /> <br /> Now the book never gives us an answer on who our beloved sheriff once was in life (as far as I know, perhaps I missed something). The truth is a mystery that I assume is up to the ST. So what I'm wondering is what identity could be so damning to the Sheriff that he strives so hard to hide it? Afterall he went by this false name even when Savoy embraced him, so clearly it is a mortal identity he has a very vested interest in hiding. But I can't help but wonder what mortal identity could be so bad that it'd have the potential to ruin Donovan. Perhaps he was a ghoul once upon a time? But if that's true then Savoy would likely have known and it seems implied no one at all knows who Donovan actually is.<br /> <br /> Beyond that our only clues seem to be the fact Donovan is not a true believer of the Lancea Sanctum and that he appears to be in his late 20s but was embraced in 1865. Doesn't really narrow things down much at all. Any opinions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","user":"Star Sage","date":". 09-03-2014, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","name":"Star Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T11:45:16-07:00","id":248057,"title":"","content":"He's John Wilkes Booth, I'm assuming. He died the same year Donovan was embraced, and, well, if that's not a dirty secret I don't know what is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T12:02:15-07:00","id":248065,"title":"","content":"Oh my god Merkonan you're right! John Wilkes booth died at age 26 which fits Donovan's age description and his death lines up perfectly with his embrace. I never would've caught that, even if that isn't the 'canon' truth that lines up so well I just have to use that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","name":"Star Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T18:56:12-07:00","id":248360,"title":"","content":"I don't know if many kindred would actually feel strongly enough about the matter for it to be a dirty secret, at least after a few decades but it's possible and i honestly have no alternatives that come even close to being this dramatic or entertaining.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T21:34:32-07:00","id":248520,"title":"","content":"If you want a member of the Kindred who'd care about it, you could introduce pre-eminent crazy american cowboy vampire Jack Cade from <i>Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners </i>if anyone is liable to care about it, it'd be him.<br /> <br /> Or TFV, maybe? Nothing says &quot;Fund our operations&quot; like bringing in a vampiric John Wilkes Booth.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-03T21:39:08-07:00","id":248523,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=248520#post248520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or TFV, maybe? Nothing says &quot;Fund our operations&quot; like bringing in a vampiric John Wilkes Booth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although, according to VALKYRIE, Booth was hired by their predecessors to kill Lincoln's body double, in order to conceal the fact that he was murdered by some sort of... <i>thing</i>. So that would be an interesting situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;These are merely stones...&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/276-merkonan","name":"Merkonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar276_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T03:52:27-07:00","id":248737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=248520#post248520\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want a member of the Kindred who'd care about it, you could introduce pre-eminent crazy american cowboy vampire Jack Cade from <i>Night Horrors: Immortal Sinners </i>if anyone is liable to care about it, it'd be him.<br /> <br /> Or TFV, maybe? Nothing says &quot;Fund our operations&quot; like bringing in a vampiric John Wilkes Booth.</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends really - not everybody sticks to &quot;TFV is a front of vampire elders&quot; as standard. Though taking down either a vampiric John Wilkes Booth or Abraham Lincoln would go a long way to justify their existence in the eyes of a number of figures in 19th century american intelligence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Merkonan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=248523#post248523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although, according to VALKYRIE, Booth was hired by their predecessors to kill Lincoln's body double, in order to conceal the fact that he was murdered by some sort of... <i>thing</i>. So that would be an interesting situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the... <i>thing </i>was a vampire or strix that would then go on to &quot;embrace&quot; Booth/Gage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-04-2014, 06:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T05:40:20-07:00","id":248763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=248737#post248737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That depends really - not everybody sticks to &quot;TFV is a front of vampire elders&quot; as standard. Though taking down either a vampiric John Wilkes Booth or Abraham Lincoln would go a long way to justify their existence in the eyes of a number of figures in 19th century american intelligence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I wasn't thinking of it from the general TFV vampire front angle, I was just thinking maybe it'd appeal to a certain sense of nationalism among command staff for them to hunt down a historically famous hemophage and show him what-for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T11:27:01-07:00","id":249013,"title":"","content":"Why wasn't this scene in <i>Abraham Lincoln Vampire Hunter</i>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ortam + Malkavia makes a Requiem fun.<br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Posts in this colour are Persuasion.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\">Posts in this colour are Seduction.</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this colour are Intimidation.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/57-solomon-birch","name":"solomon birch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar57_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"289"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T14:07:51-07:00","id":249148,"title":"","content":"I always suspected TFV (or more likely whatever earlier and much more primitive incarnation of them existed at the time) had a hand in Lincoln's death and that our beloved president may have actually been a supernatural entity himself. If that is that case I could see John Wilkes Booth serving as their 'fall guy' to lay the blame on and keep the government's hands clean.<br /> <br /> (Also just for the record, my depiction of TFV has them as an almost purely mortal organisation, they don't take orders from elders but the higher ups know that if many of those ancient vampires were to simply perish without a suitable way to handle the fallout it would often cause more harm than good.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2322,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","user":"Star Sage","date":". 09-04-2014, 05:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2322-star-sage","name":"Star Sage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2322_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T14:24:29-07:00","id":249167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Star Sage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=249148#post249148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I always suspected TFV (or more likely whatever earlier and much more primitive incarnation of them existed at the time) had a hand in Lincoln's death and that our beloved president may have actually been a supernatural entity himself. If that is that case I could see John Wilkes Booth serving as their 'fall guy' to lay the blame on and keep the government's hands clean.</div> </div> </div> </div>New World of Darkness has for the most part avoided suggesting that real historical figures were actually supernatural. It's sort of problematic in the sense that it casts implications on their dcisions or ideas which can be uncomfortable or unfair, depriving them of responsibility or agency in their decisions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Star Sage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=249148#post249148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Also just for the record, my depiction of TFV has them as an almost purely mortal organisation, they don't take orders from elders but the higher ups know that if many of those ancient vampires were to simply perish without a suitable way to handle the fallout it would often cause more harm than good.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds fairly accurate to the organization by default. If the vampire elders seem to be pulling the strings, they're doin just that, pulling strings, not commanding efforts. I think it's a fair default assumption to make that any members of TFV's Command are mortals themselves, and that if Vampire Elders have influence, it's financial influence over the organization. Or I might be misremembering <i>Compacts &amp; Conspiracies</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:11:02-07:00","id":249373,"title":"","content":"No, you're right. The basic premise seems to be that TFV, with all of it's crazy cutting-edge weapons technology, requires a lot more funding than congress would generally assign to a black budget entry that nobody seems to know anything about. As such, they get the bulk of their funding from private investors, at least some of whom are vampires who manipulate the organization into attacking their enemies while avoiding interfering with their assets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-04T19:17:24-07:00","id":249386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Star Sage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=248065#post248065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh my god Merkonan you're right! John Wilkes booth died at age 26 which fits Donovan's age description and his death lines up perfectly with his embrace. I never would've caught that, even if that isn't the 'canon' truth that lines up so well I just have to use that...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, so the sheriff was a supporter of the slave trade? Considering New Orleans' population, I can see how that would be disastrous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-27T18:31:46-07:00","id":294392,"title":"","content":"Interesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1680-justicar-seth","name":"Justicar-Seth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1680_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-04T08:40:09-08:00","id":302228,"title":"","content":"Donovan's identity started my whole chronicle. I actually took a look at the stat block for Savoy and he is full on Willpower. Seeing as other Kindred npcs who have Embraced have had their willpower adjusted (Vidal and Cimitiere come to mind) it's interesting to think that Savoy didn't Embrace Donovan.<br /> <br /> Plus. His attribute stats are very very strong for an ancillae (you could take this to model a powerful combatant threat for PCs but that's a bit ... Boring?!).<br /> <br /> Then I took a look at some of Belial's Brood powers and there is an Investment that allows a transfer of a vampiric soul from the vampire to a mortal. It got me thinking...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>VTR Chronicle on Obsidian Portal:</b> <a href=\"http://www.obsidianportal.com/campaigns/dead-of-night\" target=\"_blank\">Dead of Night ~ Tales from the Big Easy</a><br /> <br /> <b>On Onyx Path Forum:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/255-actual-play-dead-of-night\" target=\"_blank\">[ACTUAL PLAY] Dead of Night</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/44-vampdt","name":"VampDT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar44_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T20:32:44-08:00","id":316896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/248035-new-orleans-theories-donovan-s-identity?p=249386#post249386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Ah, so the sheriff was a supporter of the slave trade? Considering New Orleans' population, I can see how that would be disastrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, New Orleans is three-quarters black, going by the mortal population. That means a significant portion of the Kindred will be too, perhaps a supermajority. And factions and covenants are still roughly segregated along race lines: the Invictus's rising star is a dyed-in-the-wool white supremacist, and the faction with whom the New Orleans leadership has the most long-term tension, Cimiti\u00e8re's camp, is entirely of African descent. If Donovan ever hoped to succeed Vidal as prince, even if he lightened up on the religious restrictions, he would still need for his mortal identity to remain secret, or else he could forget about having the support of most of the city's vampires. Regardless of how much he'd changed since then, it would just be too contentious an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/352-black-flag","name":"Black Flag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar352_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-03-08T08:09:58-08:00","id":1549080,"title":"","content":"I have come very very late to the party, more than a decade (but what is a decade to those inmortal, eh?), but I'm running a pre-Katrina New Orleans game (starting with Danse de la Mort) and I was just wondering about this very secret. So, thanks everyone for the answers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26110-ramon-nogueras","name":"Ramon Nogueras","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-05-30T07:57:12-07:00","id":1551342,"title":"","content":"I love the John Wilkes Booth theory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}